  "all_ingredients_flat": "Brown Rice Paper, Water, Cauliflower, Peas, Potato, various Herbs & Spices, Ezekiel Bread Crumbs, Steel Cut Oats Bread Crumbs",
  "instructions": "BROWN RICE PAPER: Dip brown rice paper in water for a few seconds. Leaving it in for long will make it a wet mush. Then place the wet paper on a rolling platform [I used a steel rolling platform]. Use a knife to slice the paper into 2 halves.\nFILLING: Place a spoonful of sabzi on one end of the paper leaving some room to roll the paper with the sabzi (see pic). Then roll from one end to the other while gently patting both ends to ensure that it is closed and the filling doesn't fall out. Gently place the roll in the bread crumbs plate and cover it with the bread crumbs.\nBAKE: Place the rolls on a baking tray lined with parchment paper. Heat the oven at 350 F and bake the rolls for 25-30 minutes or until the outside turns crunchy.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "bake",
    "no-cook"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Enjoy with any chutneys of your choice.",
  "notes": "Brown Rice Paper - 4 [will make 8 Bread Rolls]. Cauliflower Peas & Potato Sabzi [described in its own recipe card]. Ezekiel Bread Crumbs or Steel Cut Oats Bread Crumbs [described in their own recipe cards]. [I used a steel rolling platform]. (see pic).",
